# MCP Server

Standalone app at `apps/mcp-server` — must work with Claude Desktop or any MCP client, not only our web UI.

## Required tools (mock backends OK)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `create_ticket(subject, description, priority)` | Create support ticket |
| `lookup_order_status(order_id)` | Return order status |
| `escalate_to_human(reason)` | Hand off to human agent |

## Implementation rules

- Define explicit JSON schemas for inputs and outputs.
- Validate all inputs before executing mock logic.
- Return structured responses the agent can cite in the chat UI.
- Keep auth boundaries clear even with mocks (e.g. API key env var on server start).
- Document each tool in `docs/knowledge-agent/MCP_TOOLS.md` when implemented.

## UI surfacing

Web app must show tool calls visibly: e.g. "Called `create_ticket` → ticket #4821 created".
